* FD-12  Noise
* Spec 3.2.2.6 for the FD class: capacitive gain -1 (C = {{C_NET}} F, the
* switched-capacitor application of Fig. 32); RL/CL load.  The inputs get
* their DC bias from a differential-only servo (E sources + L = 1 TH, whose
* corner with the 1 pF network is 0.16 Hz) that pins their common mode at
* VCOM: feeding each output straight back to the
* opposite input would also close a positive common-mode loop that can latch
* the amplifier off.  Noise of Vop - Von referred to VIP, 0.1 Hz .. 1 GHz.
{{SEED_OPTION}}
.lib "{{MODEL_LIB}}" {{CORNER}}
{{MC_PARAM}}
.include "{{DUT_FILE}}"
.temp {{TEMP}}
.options reltol=1e-5 abstol=1e-15 vntol=1e-9
VDD vdd 0 {{VDD}}
VSS vss 0 0
IBIAS vdd ibias {{IBIAS}}
VCM vcm 0 {{VCM}}
VIP vip vcm DC 0 AC 1
VIN vin vcm 0
C1 vip inp {{C_NET}}
C2 inp outn {{C_NET}}
C3 vin inn {{C_NET}}
C4 inn outp {{C_NET}}
EP sp vcm outn outp 0.5
EN sn vcm outp outn 0.5
LP sp inp 1T
LN sn inn 1T
XDUT vss ibias vdd vcmpin inp inn outp outn {{DUT}}
RVCM_DUT vcm vcmpin 1k
RLP outp vcm {{RL}}
CLP outp 0 {{CL}}
RLN outn vcm {{RL}}
CLN outn 0 {{CL}}
.control
set filetype=ascii
noise v(outp,outn) vip dec 20 0.1 1G
setplot noise1
write {{RAW}} onoise_spectrum inoise_spectrum
.endc
.end
